reims-vgpu: the guest linear memo skips its re-read where both write witnesses vouch.

`load_linear_guest_memoized` served a guest-CPU texture's converted copy only
after re-reading the texture's whole span out of guest memory and comparing it
byte for byte. A Home-screen swipe did that ~420-
1730 times a second over 1.1-2.9 GiB/s, every bind a hit: `sampled_resolve_split`
memo_read_us + memo_cmp_us 90-280 ms of a 105-320 ms `resolve_us`.
Now `runtime::linear_memo_witness` keeps, per memo span (bounded at 64), a guest
write tracking token over the span's pages (HostOps::track_guest_writes, the
reims-vgpu-dirty bitmap harvested at every work-handing register write) and the
`host_writes` epoch, both taken after the writeback-debt settle and before the
read that confirms the memo. A later bind is served from the memo without the
read only when: the page walk is complete and equals the watched list, the
span length and the memo's content generation are unchanged, the token's
generation is readable and unchanged, `host_writes.wrote_any_since` is Quiet
for those pages, and no submitted GPU write can still reach them. Every other
answer reads and compares exactly as before (a token is armed only for a span
the memo already holds). One vouched bind in 64 per span is read and compared
anyway; a difference fails `lin_memo_witness_unsound` and disarms the span.
`REIMS_VGPU_LINEAR_MEMO_WITNESS=off` restores the read on every bind. Routes:
lin_memo_vouched(_kb), lmw_* (refusal reasons, armed, audit_ok/unsound, evict);
`sampled_resolve_split` gains memo_witness_us/_n. Requires
reims-sampled-resolve-split.patch.
Tests: runtime::linear_memo_witness::tests (9: vouch, guest store in/out of the
span, recorded device write and unnamed write, outstanding GPU write, moved
page list/span/memo, arming window and no dirty bitmap, a store racing the
read, the audit stride and a failed audit, the bound and token release);
draw::tests::guest_linear_memo_reuses_arc_and_observes_guest_writes (third
load vouched; a guest store and a device write each observed on the next
load); draw::tests::guest_linear_memo_reads_every_load_where_guest_writes_are_unobservable.

